SUMMARY:Exercise Horizon 2026 - Observer
LOCATION:Airport Experience Centre\, Alpha Building\, 2 George Wiencke Driv
 e\, Perth Airport WA 6105
DESCRIPTION:Your observer place at Exercise Horizon 2026 is confirmed.\n\nA
 rrive 08:00 for registration and safety briefing.\nReport to: Alpha Buildi
 ng\, 2 George Wiencke Drive\, Perth Airport WA 6105 - Ground Floor\, Airpo
 rt Experience Centre (AEC).\nParking: Alpha Building car park at the AEC. 
 Use gate code 1023 to enter the staff car park. Your vehicle stays there a
 ll day and you return to it at the end.\nA map of the access gate\, the ca
 r park and the building entrance is attached to this invitation\, and is a
 lso at:\nhttps://nicholaspagonis.github.io/Exercise-Horizon-2026/assets/em
 ail/horizon-map-alpha-building.jpg\nFinish: from approximately 13:15\, fro
 m the AEC.\n\nHOW THE DAY RUNS\n08:00 - Walk in to the Alpha Building\, fo
 llow the signs to the AEC and sign in for registration\, safety briefing\,
  issue of hi-vis and conduct expectations.\n08:30 - Board the bus and trav
 el to the viewing area\, in position before the exercise commences.\n09:00
  - Observe the multi-agency response from Emergency Gate 6 and other areas
  of the airfield.\n11:30 - Move by bus to Forster Park to observe the reun
 ification process.\n12:30 - Lunch\, provided at Forster Park by the Salvat
 ion Army.\n13:15 - Return by bus to the AEC and are released to depart in 
 your own vehicle.\n\nBRING: enclosed footwear\, weather appropriate clothi
 ng\, sun protection (hat\, sunglasses and sunscreen)\, water\, photo ident
 ification\, and any personal medication you may need.\n\nPROVIDED: hi-vis 
 vest and observer lanyard\, registration and safety briefing on arrival\, 
 escorted bus transport for the full circuit\, lunch at Forster Park by the
  Salvation Army\, and on-site first aid support.\n\nYou remain escorted an
 d within the monitored viewing area at all times. Follow the directions of
  exercise staff and airport authorised officers throughout the day. Observ
 ers are photographed and filmed during the exercise.\n\nReply with any die
 tary or allergy requirements\, and let the team know as early as possible 
 if your availability changes.\nQuestions: Emergency.Exercise@perthairport.
 com.au or 0439 237 973
